# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings on every platform. A CRLF checkout (Windows git with core.autocrlf, the
# tree then built from WSL) turns the shebang into "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" and Linux stops at the first line:
# "env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory" (S. 2026-11-19, ./scripts/build-linux.sh from /mnt/c/...).
# eol=lf makes git write these with LF in every working tree, regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# bgfx shader sources (and bgfx_shader.sh above): shaderc's preprocessor on Linux rejects the CR -
# "illegal character (13 decimal) in #if" (S. 2026-11-19, the same WSL build). shaderc reads LF fine on Windows.
*.sc text eol=lf

# Other Linux-side text that breaks with CRLF (desktop entries, flatpak/appstream manifests).
*.desktop text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
